# Simulation Guidelines

## Environment Setup
The project uses Verilator with Rust bindings for simulation. Key files:
- [rust/build.rs](mdc:rust/build.rs): Verilator configuration
- [rust/src/main.rs](mdc:rust/src/main.rs): Simulation main loop
- [rtl/top_simulator.sv](mdc:rtl/top_simulator.sv): Simulation top-level

## Performance Requirements
- Target 60 FPS display refresh
- Use proper clock and reset handling
- Document all simulation parameters

## Running Simulation
Use `make run` to:
1. Build assembly code if needed
2. Compile RTL through Verilator
3. Generate Rust bindings
4. Run simulation with real-time display

## Debug Features
- VCD waveform generation
- Performance monitoring
- Frame timing analysis

## Testing
Reference [rtl/cpu6502_tb.sv](mdc:rtl/cpu6502_tb.sv) for testbench structure:
- Clear test case documentation
- Comprehensive coverage
- Edge case handling
- Timing verification
